Here’s a comprehensive `.gitignore` file for a Python project. It covers Python artifacts, virtual environments, IDE settings, testing, environment variables, logs, and build files.

gitignore

````gitignore

# ==============================
# Python
# ==============================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.python-version

# ==============================
# Virtual Environments
# ==============================
venv/
env/
ENV/
.venv/
.virtualenv/

# ==============================
# Environment Variables & Secrets
# ==============================
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets.json

# ==============================
# Distribution / Packaging
# ==============================
build/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
MANIFEST

# ==============================
# Testing & Coverage
# ==============================
.pytest_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
nosetests.xml
junit.xml
test-results/

# ==============================
# Type Checking & Linting
# ==============================
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
.pyre/
.pytype/
.ruff_cache/
.pyright/

# ==============================
# Jupyter Notebook
# ==============================
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb_checkpoints

# ==============================
# IDEs & Editors
# ==============================
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ==============================
# Logs & Temporary Files
# ==============================
*.log
logs/
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp

# ==============================
# Operating Systems
# ==============================
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ==============================
# Python Build Tools
# ==============================
pip-wheel-metadata/
poetry.toml

# ==============================
# Frameworks
# ==============================
instance/
.webassets-cache/

# Django
*.pot
local_settings.py
db.sqlite3
db.sqlite3-journal
media/

# Flask
instance/

# ==============================
# Celery
# ==============================
celerybeat-schedule
celerybeat.pid

# ==============================
# PyInstaller
# ==============================
*.manifest
*.spec

# ==============================
# Miscellaneous
# ==============================
.cache/
.pybuild/
site/
```

**Usage:**
1. Create a file named `.gitignore` in your project's root directory.
2. Paste the contents above.
3. Save and commit it to Git.

**Tip:** Keep `.env.example` in Git so other developers know which environment variables they need, but never commit your actual `.env` file.
````